Dialogue: {
	Soulless: {
		Introduction: So another bearer wakes. Keep close the souls you gather; death is eager to loosen your grasp.
		BloodstainHint: What spills from you does not vanish. Return to the stain, reach into it, and take back what remains.
		AfterKingSlime: Even a crown of gel leaves an echo. The Terraforge can press that echo into useful form.
		FragmentSale: This edge remembers a blade older than either of us. Drive it into an anvil, and the metal will learn to shape what flesh leaves behind.
		BuriedCourtHint: Take this fragment. The reliquary remembers the office, not the hand. Let the prisoners mistake you for their keeper.
		AfterCongregation: So the court is silent. Strange... I remember every voice you freed, though none of them were mine.
	}

	Court: {
		ReliquaryAccepts: The reliquary accepts an authority it should not remember.
		CongregationDeath: The final voices fade: The hand behind the mark... is hollow.
	}
}

